R-PB9 R-PB3 R-PB7 R-PP3 R-J4 R-J5 R-J6 R-OUT2 (slice 217b, Design Q580, Q581): `data.facts` of `tln probe --range --json`: the real facts that this run probed, as `{nightly, target, result}`, in the probe order. `facts` is the last key of `data` (and of `error.details`, see `probe/pc2-range` run E and `probe/pd1-downloads` run 8). It is always there. The world is that of `probe/pc2-range` (packages, compiler list n1 to n10, installed n1, n3, n5 to n10, the config, the truth of the fake `units`). 5 runs in one home, so the db of run 3 has the facts of runs 1 and 2.
Run 1 (setup, as run A of `pc2-range`): parser in p2 with `probe.max` 4, no `--json`. Round 1 probes n10, n9, n8 and round 2 probes n3. The facts are saved, exit 12 (budget). Its output has no `facts`.
Run 2 (R-PB9 "not the facts that compat.db had before", R-PB3, R-PP3): parser in p1 with `--json`, as run B of `pc2-range`. The db has the 4 facts of run 1. The search probes n5, n6, n7 (one round, in the order of the list: fail, pass, pass). `facts` has these 3, in this order, and none of the 4 stored facts. Both ends are real (n5 is a real fail, n10 is the end of D): exit 0, `ok` true.
Run 3 (R-PB9 "not the inferred facts", R-PP3, R-J5): `--range <bundle file> --json`, as run F of `pc2-range`: 3 rounds, 7 probes (n10 n9 n8, n3 n5 n6, n1), all pass. The releases n2, n4 and n7 have inferred passes (R-EP6): they are not in `facts`. The 7 facts are in the order of the probes (round by round, the order of the list in a round). Exit 0.
Run 4 (Q581 item 1): run 3 again. All facts are known, no probe starts, the range is the same, exit 0: `facts` is `[]`, and the member is there.
Run 5 (Q581 item 3): the bundle AJn26 (a hash that fails on each compiler of the list). The db has stored fails for n2 and n4 (they are not installed); the 8 installed compilers are probed in 3 rounds (n10 n9 n8, n7 n6 n5, n3 n1) and all fail. Every release has a real fail, so the result is no pass with no unseen release: exit 0 (`ProbeCmd.stop` row 6), `range` is `null`, and `data.facts` has the 8 probed facts and not the 2 stored ones.
The target of each fact is `any`, the target of the key of a unit check (Q581 item 4, R-P4).
